02:21:57,934 --> 02:22:02,592
We're gonna fix it by using Sentry, which is completely free to get started with.

1602
02:22:02,912 --> 02:22:06,884
So think of it like the watchtower of your application.

1603
02:22:07,232 --> 02:22:13,792
Now it is much more than just error tracking and monitoring, but here are some of the things that I can highlight.

1604
02:22:13,952 --> 02:22:25,604
So it's going to catch the errors, it's going to show us the structured logs, which is like console.log, but it is structured, that means you know it is searchable and it is persisted in the cloud.

1605
02:22:25,792 --> 02:22:32,352
Then there are session replays, which means that it's gonna take video recording anytime there is an error.

1606
02:22:32,526 --> 02:22:36,192
So let's say your user presses button and it has failed.

1607
02:22:36,398 --> 02:22:40,992
So you will have the video recording of that in your sentry dashboard.

1608
02:22:41,294 --> 02:22:49,552
Then it helps with performance, such as traces and bottlenecks, and as I have already mentioned, you're going to get real-time alerts.

